## F2 (continuation) - authorized adj_ratio deviation, rerun, snapshot frozen

- **Date:** 2026-11-23
- **Task:** F2 continuation after HARD stop. User explicitly authorized Option 1 (scoped spec/check change for yfinance adj_ratio precision artifact). No silent fix.
- **What changed and why:** Investigation showed adj_ratio HARDs were ~1e-6..1.6e-6 relative drifts on non-dividend/non-split days (bond ETFs prominent), consistent with yfinance Adj Close/Close precision artifacts, while dividend days showed expected ratio steps. With explicit user authorization, `check_adj_ratio` tolerance was changed from `1e-6` to `1e-4` in `backend/app/research/data_quality.py` (docstring/comment/log note added). This is a deliberate, logged deviation from F1 text; no other check/threshold weakened. Re-ran snapshot script; it passed.
- **Files touched:**
  - `backend/app/research/data_quality.py` (edited - authorized deviation)
  - `scripts/research_etf_snapshot.py` (created earlier in F2)
  - `docs/backtests/research/ETF_DATA_QUALITY.md` (regenerated)
  - `research_data/etf_20261124/` (20 csv.gz + manifest.json)
  - `.github/workflows/research.yml` (edited earlier in F2)
  - `docs/SESSIONS/research-etf-log.nd` (appended)

